## Worksheet

**F1 Core loop**: single `S` object; `R()` reads/writes `S.rngState` for all in-game randomness; `runTurn()` calls stormPhase→production→needsPhase→eventsPhase→caravanPhase→checkEnd in fixed order. Score 2.

**F2 Map**: `genMap(seed)` builds 64-tile grid via seeded `mkRng`; `tryBuild` checks `d.terr.includes(map[i])`; `adjCount` drives real output multipliers (condenser/greenhouse/forge). Score 2.

**F3 Economy**: sifter→soil, greenhouse consumes 2 soil+water→food, mine→ore, forge consumes 3 ore+power→metal, workshop consumes 2 metal+power→parts; `caps()`/`addRes` enforce caps with overflow logging. Score 2.

**F4 Population**: colonist records `{skill,fatigue,morale,job,b}`; `workerMult()` reads `c.skill`/`c.fatigue`/`c.morale` in `production()`. Score 2.

**F5 Needs**: `needsPhase` computes food/water shortage → `dm-=12/-10` morale hit; `workerMult` reads morale (<40 ×0.7, 0 refuses); recovery via `dm=2+...` when unmet needs absent. Score 2.

**F6 Research**: `RESEARCH` has 10 nodes; `tryResearch` enforces `node.req.every(has)` and deducts cost; effects (`filters`,`bore`,`drip`,`turbine`,`heatx`,`barter`,`shield`,`depots`,`medbay`,`salvage`) all read elsewhere. Score 2.

**F7 Events**: `EVENTS` array has 12 entries; weighted roll in `eventsPhase`; 6 events with 2-3 differing-outcome choices; `s.cds[id]=EVENT_COOLDOWN` checked via pool filter. Score 2.

**F8 Trade**: `priceOf` reads `s.res[g]/cap` scarcity and `s.drift[g]` (random-walked each turn in `caravanPhase`); `cv.inv[g]` limited and decremented; `tradeDeal` handles both buy/sell. Score 2.

**F9 Hazard**: `stormPhase` fires every 8 turns, `sev=1+floor(turn/20)` grows; `production()` halves output at hp<50, disables at hp<=0; `shield`/walls mitigate; `tryRepair` spends 2 parts+1 metal+idle labor, restores hp. Score 2.

**F10 Save/load**: `exportSave` serializes `stripUi(S)` to JSON text; `importSave` parses, validates required fields/types, returns clear error string shown in `#saveerr`. Score 2.

**F11 End conditions**: `checkEnd` has win (`colonists>=12 && !shortage` at turn60) and lose (`colonists.length===0`), both reachable; `score()` combines pop/research/turns/stockpile; `renderModal` shows summary table. Score 2.

**F12 UI**: `switchTab` wires tab buttons; log lines show `T${e.t}`; extensive title tooltips explain formulas; Space/1-5 keyboard shortcuts; `@media(max-width:420px)` layout adjustments. Score 2.

**F13 Dev panel**: `runTests()` asserts real invariants (cap enforcement, prereqs, overflow clamp, starvation departures, save/load hash match, research changing yield); `runBench()` runs 200 headless turns via `greedyTurn`, prints `stateHash`. Score 2.

**G1**: `has(s,"filters")` read directly inside condenser branch of `production()`, same pattern for bore/drip/turbine/heatx — fully wired every turn. Score 4.

**G2**: `needsPhase` shortage → `c.morale` drop → next-turn `production()`'s `workerMult` reads morale to cut/zero output. Full traceable loop. Score 4.

**G3**: `stormPhase` damages `b.hp` → `production()` halves/disables output → `tryRepair` spends parts+metal+labor → `b.hp=100` restores output. Score 4.

**G4**: `priceOf` reads `s.res[g]/caps(s)[g]` scarcity and `s.drift[g]`, drift updated by random walk in `caravanPhase` each turn. Score 4.

**G5**: refugees/wreck/thieves/festival choice branches each write distinct `s.res`, `s.colonists` mutations (not just `logMsg`). Score 4.

